/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-------------------------------*\
  envelope03_c3c4c5_both_stop -- the same C3/C4/C5 feed as envelope02,
  marched to 80 bar instead of 40: BOTH branches stop, and the run says where
  and why.

  WHY THIS CASE EXISTS (2026-11-15).  envelope02 was the corpus witness of a
  stopped branch until C245 (2026-11-08); since then both of its branches
  reach the top of its 1-40 bar range, so no case in the corpus showed a
  branch that STOPS.  The Explorer's envelope lens is built around that
  report -- a stopped branch must never look like a closed envelope or like a
  solver failure -- and its test needs an engine run in which a stop
  happens.  This is that run, on the lens's own frame (an ideal liquid on the
  pure-liquid reference, a Peng-Robinson vapour, kij = 0 announced).

  WHAT THE RUN SHOWS (native build, 2026-11-15):

    * the bubble branch keeps 44 points and stops at 45 bar (last kept point
      395.780 K at 44 bar).  It stopped at 64 bar until 2026-11-15, when
      T_bubble priced the vapour at the liquid's own composition (y = x,
      EX-04); it now iterates the incipient vapour, which is about 63 %
      propane and nears its own pseudo-critical region (about 395 K and
      40 bar on Kay's rule) there -- P_bubble on this package jumps between
      vapour roots above 397 K for the same reason, so 45 bar is where the
      iterated vapour stops being a vapour, not a tolerance;
    * the dew branch keeps 46 points and stops at 47 bar (last kept point
      408.151 K at 46 bar);
    * both stops are reported as a pressure-marched trace running out of
      single-valuedness (the cricondenbar or the critical region), not as a
      root jump, and no cricondentherm is claimed: neither branch has an
      interior temperature maximum in what it kept.

  WHAT IT DOES NOT SHOW.  The last kept points are 395.780 K (bubble, 44
  bar) and 408.151 K (dew, 46 bar), on either side of the nose of this feed;
  the op does not close it
  (Michelsen's continuation is not implemented) and in this frame the liquid
  is not described by the equation of state, so the frame has no mixture
  critical point of its own.  The stopping pressures are properties of the
  METHOD on this frame, not measured features of the mixture.

  NOT VALIDATED: no number here is checked against a measured envelope.  This
  is a STRUCTURAL witness for the stop report; its counts and stopping
  pressures are the golden rows.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoProps;
description  "P-T envelope of a C3/C4/C5 feed marched to 80 bar on an ideal liquid and a PR vapour: the bubble branch stops at 45 bar and the dew branch at 47 bar, each reported in the engine's words, and no cricondentherm is claimed";
verbosity     3;
